<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pangeran Benawa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pangeran Benawa was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadiwijaya">Hadiwijaya</a>, the first sultan of Pajang in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-java">Central Java</a>. After his father's death in 1582 the throne was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arya-pangiri">Arya Pangiri</a> of Demak, but in 1586 Benawa and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panembahan-senapati">Sutawijaya</a> of Mataram deposed him. Benawa then ruled Pajang briefly, under the growing power of Mataram.</p></div>
